# The annotations of music/music (kit/mkgame.py --part src/music/music.json). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
#
# The image: TZX block 4 $6000-$71FF, copied by the 128K setup ($7200 in page 5, c1 frames 11790-11841) to RAM 6
# $C000-$D1FF and run there. Ben Daglish's AY player (the ZXDB AY rip, work/candidates/zxdb-info/Terramex.ay.zip,
# names "Benn Daglish", one song, init = play = $C000) and its tunes.
# Witness: "L1 N (builds)" is the runs of an entry's first instruction summed over the part's recordings (music.json
# "l1": c1, explorers, gameover and the 31 rzx pieces); kit/mkgame.py --fix-witness writes the real counts.
# "Known only from the code" marks what no recording ran or read. No instruction outside RAM 6 reads or writes these
# bytes after the copy (every page-6 writer in the 34 recordings is a page-6 routine, the copy $7200 or, before it,
# the ROM's power-on RAM clear $00C7).
# Pitch: a pattern note n plays period-table index n + 20 + transpose; index i is MIDI note i + 12 (index 0 = C0,
# 16.35 Hz at the 128K's AY clock of 1.7734 MHz), so note n at transpose 0 is MIDI n + 32 (note 0 = G#1).

@isub $C51E LD BC,VibratoTable-8
@isub $C631 LD BC,VibratoTable-8

@module player ; The player's entry, the start and the end of a tune, the frame update
@about MusicFrame $C000 is the only entry the game uses: the IM 2 handler $9491 pages RAM 6 ($7FFD = $16) and calls it at every interrupt when Has128K $5FFE is not 0 (no music on a 48K), from GameEntry $8F00 on (c1: GameEntry frame 21597, the first call frame 21599) through the selector, the play, the game over and the ending. MusicTick $C014 starts tune 0 (StartTune $C79F) when PlayerState $C027 is 0, else runs UpdateTune $C1E4. The image's PlayerState is 0, so the first call starts tune 0; EndTune $C780 sets it to 0 at the tune's end, so the next call starts tune 0 again.
@about Who selects a tune: nobody. StartTune takes the tune number in A, but its only caller is the JP Z at $C018 with A = 0, and no code outside RAM 6 writes PlayerState, TuneNumberOp+1 or TunePointer (the game's only calls into $C000 are $94A0, the music, and $8F5E, which pages RAM 1 and calls the explorer selector). So Terramex plays tune 0 and only tune 0, in a loop of 9698 frames (9696 frames of notes, the end frame and the start frame; 3 min 14 s at 50 Hz): EndTune ran at frames 9581 (explorers), 1676 (r08000), 1374 (r18000), 1072 (r28000), 770 (r38000), 468 (r48000), 9698 frames apart through the RZX run. The tune table has four entries: 0, 2 and 3 are the same tune, 1 is a shorter tune made of tune 0's second half (known only from the code).
@about Sound effects: the player plays none. Its AY writes are the only ones in the 34 recordings after the ROM's power-on set-up (AYWrite $CD56 is the one routine with ports $FFFD / $BFFD); the game's effects are beeper sounds through port $FE (the game's sound module).
@about A frame (UpdateTune): for each channel whose note timer is 1 the note ends now (timer 0, NoteEndFlag $C14D up); then channels A, B and C in turn (UpdateChannel $C2E4 with IX = the channel record, DE = its pattern, the four self-modified order-list operands and SlotRowOp set for the channel); then WriteAY $C290, except on a frame where a note ended (NoteEndFlag not 0: the AY keeps the last frame's values and no channel runs its effects). 3590 T-states a frame on average (explorers: 54 533 870 T-states in 15 190 calls).

$C000 c MusicFrame ; Play one frame of music: the IM 2 handler's call
> Saves AF (in AF'), AF', DE, HL, IX and IY around MusicTick $C014 and returns with them. BC is not saved: the caller, the IM 2 handler $9491, saves it (PUSH BC at $9498) and pages RAM 6 before the CALL $C000 at $94A0 and the old page ($5FE5 Last7FFD) after it.
> Called once a frame: c1 runs it 5029 times in the 5029 frames from 21599 to 26627; explorers 15 190 of 15 190, gameover 6000 of 6000.
> Witness: L1 83616 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

$C014 c MusicTick ; Start tune 0 if no tune is playing, else play one frame of it
> PlayerState $C027 = 0: JP StartTune $C79F with A = 0 (the tune number), which returns to MusicFrame. Else UpdateTune $C1E4 with IY saved.
> c1 runs StartTune once (frame 21599, the first call after GameEntry); explorers and the rzx pieces once after each EndTune.
> Witness: L1 83616 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C018 ; A = 0 here: the only tune StartTune is ever given
$C01D ; IY = 0: not read; SetInstrument $C3D8 sets IY before every use

@module state ; The player's state: the instruments, the instrument slots, the channel records
@about Instruments $C028: 27 records of 9 bytes, of which records 0-10 are real and 11-26 blank. A record: +0, +1 not read (+1 is 8 in every record); +2 bit 7: noise (the channel's tone off, noise on; bit 7 clear: tone on, noise off; the other bits are not read: the values $11, $17, $21, $41, $81 are those of the C64 SID's waveform register, $81 noise); +3 the attack (high nibble) and decay (low nibble) rates, +4 the sustain level (high nibble) and the release rate (low nibble), each rate an index into AttackRates $CD36 or DecayRates $CD46 (0: the whole step, 15, in one frame); +5 the gate-off time: the release starts when the note timer reaches it (2 in every record); +6 not read; +7 the vibrato: an offset into VibratoTable-8 (0 none); +8 the peak volume (0-15) the attack climbs to.
@about A pattern's instrument command $8n takes slot n of the channel: SlotTable $C11B + 8 x channel + n holds the record's offset (9 x record) from Instruments. SlotTable starts as records 0-7 in slots 0-7 for every channel; the order-list command $E0+n, m writes m into slot n of the channel and the change stays: StartTune does not reset SlotTable, so tune 0's second and later passes start with channel B's slot 0 = record 8 (noise) and slot 6 = record 10 (peak 12), where the first pass had records 0 and 6 (explorers writes $C123 and $C129 at frames 5621-8645, the first EndTune at 9581).
@about A channel record (45 bytes: ChannelA $C153, ChannelB $C180, ChannelC $C1AD; StartTune clears all three): +$00 the order-list position, +$01 the transpose (signed, in semitones), +$02 the pattern position, +$03 the note timer (frames left; 0: read the next event), +$04 the pattern repeats left, +$06 the gate-off time, +$09 the detune (added to the period), +$0A the vibrato delay or cycles, +$0B the vibrato record offset, +$0C the vibrato step (bits 0-6, 1-7) and direction (bit 7), +$10 the arpeggio record offset (8n, 0 none), +$11 the slide count ($FF endless), +$12/$13 the slide step, +$14 the slide delay, +$15 the slide command byte (bit 5 the direction), +$16 the rest timer, +$17 the arpeggio step ($FF, $FE: ended), +$18 the arpeggio hold, +$1C the note's period-table index, +$1D/$1E the tone period, +$1F the volume (0-15), +$20 the sustain level, +$21/$22/$23 the decay step, rate (bit 7: done) and counter, +$24/$25/$26 the same for the attack, +$27/$28/$29 for the release, +$2A bit 0 the gate (1 attack/decay/sustain, 0 release), +$2B the peak volume. +$05, +$07, +$08, +$0D-$0F, +$19-$1B and +$2C are not used.

$C027 b PlayerState 1 ; 0: start tune 0 at the next call; 1: a tune is playing
> Read by MusicTick $C014 and UpdateTune $C1E4, set to 1 by StartTune $C79F, to 0 by EndTune $C780. The image holds 0, so the first call after the copy starts tune 0. Explorers writes it at frames 9581 and 9582 (the tune's end and the restart).

$C028 b Instruments 9 ; The instruments: 27 records of 9 bytes (the shape in the module's header)
> Selected through SlotTable by SetInstrument $C3D8 (IY = the record). Rates below are AttackRates/DecayRates entries: "n/f" n volume steps a frame, "1/nf" one step every n frames. Who uses a record is tune 0's use (the channel and pattern). Every real record has sustain 0, release index 10 (1/5f; with the gate off 2 frames before a note's end the release never steps: its code $C5F0 ran in no recording) and gate-off time 2.
> Witness: the recordings read records 0 and 2-10 (records 1 and 11-26 are read in none).
@res music/instruments.bin
$C028 ; record 0: tone; attack instant; decay 13 (1/28f); peak 15. Channels A and B slot 0: the bass of patterns 0, 3 and 15
$C031 ; record 1: tone ($17); decay 13; peak 15. Slot 1: only pattern 1 (tune 1) and pattern 4 (no tune) select it
$C03A ; record 2: noise; decay 6 (2/f); peak 15. Channel C slot 2: the noise rhythm of pattern 2
$C043 ; record 3: tone; decay 8 (1/f); peak 15. Slot 3: pattern 5
$C04C ; record 4: tone; attack 7 (4/f); decay 12 (1/9f); vibrato 8; peak 15. Channel B slot 4: the melody of pattern 6
$C055 ; record 5: tone ($21); decay 7 (1/f); vibrato 8; peak 15. Channel C slot 5: patterns 7-9
$C05E ; record 6: tone; decay 9 (1/2f); peak 15. Slot 6: patterns 10, 11, 13, 16, 18, 19
$C067 ; record 7: as record 4. Channel C slot 7: the melody of patterns 14, 17 and 20
$C070 ; record 8: noise; decay 9 (1/2f); peak 15. Channel B slot 0 after E0 48: the noise beats of patterns 13 and 16 (with arpeggio 6)
$C079 ; record 9: tone ($11); decay 9; peak 13. Channel B slot 6 after E6 51: pattern 19, the fade
$C082 ; record 10: tone ($11); decay 9; peak 12. Channel B slot 6 after E6 5A: pattern 19, the fade
$C08B ; records 11-26: blank (+2 = 0: tone; every rate 0; +8 = 15 in record 11, 0 in the rest)

$C11B b SlotTable 8 ; The instrument slots: 8 x channel + slot -> the record's offset (9 x record) in Instruments
> Read by SetInstrument $C3D8 (index 8 x channel + n, n 0-15), written by SetSlot $C7F7 (8 x channel + n, n 0-31), so 48 bytes: rows 0-2 are channels A, B and C, rows 3-5 are reached only by an n beyond the channel's 8 slots (no tune does).
> Witness: the recordings read channel A slots 0, 3, 6, channel B 0, 3, 4, 6, channel C 2, 5, 6, 7; explorers writes $C123 (B slot 0: $48, record 8) and $C129 (B slot 6: $51, then $5A).
@res music/slots.bin
$C11B ; channel A slots 0-7
$C123 ; channel B slots 0-7
$C12B ; channel C slots 0-7
$C133 ; past channel C: not read in any recording

$C14B w TunePointer 1 ; The current tune's entry in TuneTable
> Set by StartTune $C79F (TuneTable + 6 x tune), read by UpdateTune $C1E4 for each channel's order list.

$C14D b NoteEndFlag 1 ; Not 0: a note ended this frame (no effects, no AY write)
> UpdateTune $C1E4 adds 1 for each channel whose note timer is 1 at the frame's start (the timer is set to 0 there, so the channel reads its next event this frame). ChannelEffects $C56D returns before the envelope and the effects, UpdateTune skips WriteAY $C290, and UpdateTuneEnd $C2DF clears the flag. explorers: 1778 of 15 189 updates skip the AY write.

$C14E b MixerImage 1 ; The AY mixer (register 7) the player writes: $B8 at the start
> Bits 0-2 tone off, 3-5 noise off for channels A, B, C, set by SetInstrument $C3D8 from the instrument's +2 bit 7; bits 6-7 stay %10 from the image. Written to register 7 by WriteAY $C2CB.

$C14F b PlayerSpare 4 ; Not used: $0F and three zeros
> No instruction reads or writes it (known only from the code).

$C153 b ChannelA 15 ; Channel A's record (45 bytes, the fields in the module's header)
> IX for channel A in UpdateTune $C1E4; cleared by StartTune $C79F. WriteAY $C290 reads the period and the volume, EndTune $C780 zeroes the volume.
$C156 ChannelATimer ; +$03 the note timer, tested by UpdateTune
$C170 ChannelAPeriod ; +$1D/+$1E the tone period: AY registers 0 and 1
$C172 ChannelAVolume ; +$1F the volume: AY register 8

$C180 b ChannelB 15 ; Channel B's record
> As ChannelA, AY registers 2, 3 and 9.
$C183 ChannelBTimer ; +$03 the note timer
$C19D ChannelBPeriod ; +$1D/+$1E the tone period: AY registers 2 and 3
$C19F ChannelBVolume ; +$1F the volume: AY register 9

$C1AD b ChannelC 15 ; Channel C's record
> As ChannelA, AY registers 4, 5 and 10 (written only while tune 0 plays, TuneNumberOp $C2AE).
$C1B0 ChannelCTimer ; +$03 the note timer
$C1CA ChannelCPeriod ; +$1D/+$1E the tone period: AY registers 4 and 5
$C1CC ChannelCVolume ; +$1F the volume: AY register 10

$C1DA w PatternPointers 3 ; The pattern each channel is playing (A, B, C)
> Set to EmptyPattern $C82D by StartTune $C79F, to a pattern by StartPattern $C34A (PatternLo/PatternHi), read by UpdateTune $C1E4 into DE.

$C1E0 b CommandParam 1 ; A scratch byte: an order command's parameter, then a vibrato step's size
> ReadOrderList $C32A writes the low 5 bits of an order-list command for SetRepeat $C81B and SetSlot $C7F7; VibratoStep $C636 keeps the step's size there.

$C1E1 b PlayerSpare2 2 ; Not used: two zeros
> No instruction reads or writes it (known only from the code).

$C1E3 b ChannelIndex 1 ; The channel being updated: 0 A, 1 B, 2 C
> Set by UpdateTune $C1E4, read by StartPattern $C34B (PatternPointers) and SetInstrument $C3F6 (the mixer bits).

@module player
$C1E4 c UpdateTune ; Play one frame of the tune: end the expiring notes, update channels A, B and C, write the AY
> Called by MusicTick $C014 while PlayerState $C027 is 1 (the RET Z at $C1E8 is a second guard: it never returns there in any recording).
> First, for each channel whose note timer (+$03) is 1: the timer becomes 0 and NoteEndFlag $C14D goes up, so the note lasts exactly its duration in frames and the channel reads its next event this frame. Then for each channel n = 0, 1, 2: ChannelIndex $C1E3 = n, SlotRowOp+1 = 8n, IX = the channel's record, the word n of the tune's entry (TunePointer $C14B) into the operands of OrderListOp1 $C315, OrderListOp2 $C7D6, OrderListOp3 $C7E9 and OrderListOp4 $C807, DE = PatternPointers[n]; CALL UpdateChannel $C2E4. Last, H = $FF and L = $BF (the high bytes of the AY ports $FFFD and $BFFD), C = $FD, and WriteAY $C290 unless NoteEndFlag is up.
> Out: the channel records, PatternPointers and the AY registers updated, NoteEndFlag 0. When channel A meets its order list's end, EndTune $C780 drops UpdateChannel's return, so channels B and C are not updated that frame.
> Witness: L1 83609 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C1E9 ; HL = NoteEndFlag
$C1EC ; channel A's timer 1: 0, and the flag up
$C1F6 UpdateTuneB ; channel B's timer
$C200 UpdateTuneC ; channel C's timer
$C20A UpdateTuneChannels ; channel A: index 0, slot row 0
$C215 ; the tune's word 0: channel A's order list, into the four self-modified operands
$C228 ; DE = channel A's pattern
$C22F ; channel B: index 1, the tune's word 1, slot row 8
$C259 ; channel C: index 2, the tune's word 2, slot row 16
$C285 ; the AY port high bytes in H and L, the low byte in C
$C28A ; a note ended this frame: no AY write

@module ay ; The AY registers: the frame's write and the port access
@about WriteAY $C290 writes registers 0-5 (the tone periods of A, B, C), 10 (C's volume), 7 (MixerImage $C14E), 8 and 9 (the volumes of A and B), in that order, through AYWrite $CD56 (register select at port $FFFD, the value at $BFFD). Channel C's registers 4, 5 and 10 are written only for tune 0 (TuneNumberOp $C2AE: CP 1, JR NC), so a tune other than 0 would leave channel C free; tune 0 is the only one played. The noise period (6) and the envelope (11-13) are never written: noise instruments sound at the period the ROM's power-on set-up left (known only from the code). Volumes are 0-15, never the envelope mode bit (no peak is above 15).

$C290 c WriteAY ; Write the periods, the mixer and the volumes to the AY
> In: H = $FF, L = $BF, C = $FD (the ports for AYWrite $CD56). Reached from UpdateTune $C1E4 when NoteEndFlag $C14D is 0, and from EndTune $C780 (the silence at the tune's end; it jumps here whatever the flag). Falls into EndFrame $C2DF.
> explorers: 13 411 writes in 15 190 frames (the other 1778 frames a note ended).
> Witness: L1 73906 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C290 ; registers 0 and 1: channel A's period
$C2A0 ; registers 2 and 3: channel B's period
$C2AE TuneNumberOp ; LD A,n: n = the tune playing (self-modified by StartTune $C7A0; always 0): channel C only for tune 0
$C2B4 ; registers 4 and 5: channel C's period
$C2C1 ; register 10: channel C's volume
$C2C9 WriteAYMixer ; register 7: the mixer
$C2D1 ; registers 8 and 9: the volumes of A and B

$C2DF c EndFrame ; Clear NoteEndFlag: the frame's update is over
> Reached by WriteAY $C290 falling in and by UpdateTune's JR NZ at $C28E (a frame with no AY write). Returns to MusicTick $C014, UpdateTune's caller (after EndTune too, which dropped UpdateChannel's return).
> Witness: L1 83609 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

@module channel ; A channel's frame: the events of its order list and its patterns
@about Each channel has an order list (the tune's entry gives its three addresses) of bytes: $00-$7F play pattern n (PatternLo $CA37 / PatternHi $CA52, 27 patterns); $80 t: transpose t (signed semitones) for the following patterns; $A0+n: play the next pattern n times (n 0: 256); $C0 d: detune d (0-255, added to the 16-bit period) for the following notes; $E0+n m: instrument slot n of this channel = record offset m (SlotTable); $FF: the tune's end (EndTune $C780, from whichever channel meets it first: channel A in tune 0). Bits 0-4 of a command byte are its parameter, bits 5-6 pick the handler (ReadOrderList $C310), so $81-$9F take a byte as $80 does, and $C1-$DF as $C0.
@about A pattern (PatternEvent $C36D) is a string of events ended by $FF: $00-$7F n, d: a note (period-table index n + 20 + transpose) lasting d frames (d 0: 256); $A0 d: a rest of d frames (period 0, the volume left as it was); $80-$8F: instrument slot 0-15 (SetInstrument $C3D8: SlotTable row of the channel); $90-$9F, $A1-$BE: arpeggio n = the low nibble (record 8n of ArpeggioTable $C927, 0 off); $BF: the slide off; $C0-$FE s lo hi c: a slide (SlideEffect $C72F) with delay s & $1F frames after each note start, step hi:lo (halved), count c frames ($FF endless; a finite slide stops at the next note), direction bit 5 (1: period up, the pitch falls). Events other than notes and rests take no time: a channel reads on until a note or a rest.
@about Timing: a note or rest of d frames is read on frame t, its timer counts down, and the next event is read on frame t + d (UpdateTune ends the note when the timer is 1). A channel starts on EmptyPattern $C82D ($FF), so its first frame goes to the order list. The tune is a fixed grid: tune 0's channels A and B take 9696 frames, its channel C 10 236 (its last 540 frames are never heard: channel A's end stops the tune first).

$C2E4 c UpdateChannel ; Play one frame of the channel IX: the next event when its note is over, else the effects
> In: IX = the channel record, DE = its pattern (PatternPointers), the order-list operands and SlotRowOp set by UpdateTune $C1E4. Timer (+$03) not 0: CheckGateOff $C555 (the effects). Timer 0: a slide whose count is not $FF ends (+$11 = 0), then ReadPatternEvent $C2F6.
> Called 3 times a frame by UpdateTune (explorers: 45 565 = 3 x 15 189 less 2, the frame of EndTune).
> Witness: L1 250815 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C2E8 ; a note or a rest is running
$C2EB ; the slide count: $FF keeps it, any other value ends it

$C2F6 c ReadPatternEvent ; Read the byte at the channel's pattern position: an event, or the pattern's end
> HL = DE + the pattern position (+$02). Not $FF: PatternEvent $C36D. $FF: repeats left (+$04 not 0): one less, the position 0, read again; else ReadOrderList $C310. Reached from UpdateChannel $C2E4 and, after each event that takes no time, from PatternEvent's handlers and StartPattern $C34A.
> Witness: L1 21280 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C2FD ; $FF: the pattern's end
$C301 ; repeats left: the pattern again from its start

$C310 c ReadOrderList ; Read the channel's next order-list byte: a pattern, a command or the tune's end
> The byte at the order list (the self-modified operand of OrderListOp1) + the position (+$00), the position one on. $FF: EndTune $C780. $00-$7F: StartPattern $C34A. $80-$FE: CommandParam $C1E0 = the low 5 bits; bits 5-6 x 4 into the JR offset at OrderCommandJump+1: $80-$9F SetTranspose $C7E4, $A0-$BF SetRepeat $C81B (OrderJumpRepeat $C33F), $C0-$DF SetDetune $C7D1 (OrderJumpDetune $C343), $E0-$FE SetSlot $C7F7 (OrderJumpSlot $C347). Each handler comes back here for the next byte.
> Witness: L1 873 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C315 OrderListOp1 ; LD BC,nn: nn = the channel's order list (self-modified by UpdateTune; the image holds tune 0's channel A)
$C31D ; $FF: the tune's end
$C322 ; bit 7 clear: a pattern number
$C327 ; a command: the parameter, then bits 5-6 as the jump
$C339 OrderCommandJump ; JR d: d = 0, 4, 8 or 12 (self-modified at $C336; the image holds $FE, a jump to itself)
$C33B ; d = 0, $80-$9F: SetTranspose

$C33E b OrderJumpPad1 1 ; A filler byte: the jump table's entries are 4 bytes apart
> Never executed or read: JR d lands on the JP after it (known only from the code).

$C33F c OrderJumpRepeat ; d = 4, $A0-$BF: SetRepeat
> Witness: L1 123 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

$C342 b OrderJumpPad2 1 ; A filler byte between the jumps
> Never executed or read (known only from the code).

$C343 c OrderJumpDetune ; d = 8, $C0-$DF: SetDetune
> Witness: L1 17 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

$C346 b OrderJumpPad3 1 ; A filler byte between the jumps
> Never executed or read (known only from the code).

$C347 c OrderJumpSlot ; d = 12, $E0-$FE: SetSlot
> Witness: L1 21 (explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

$C34A c StartPattern ; Start pattern A on the channel
> A = the pattern number (0-26, from ReadOrderList $C310). PatternPointers[ChannelIndex] = DE = PatternLo[A] + 256 x PatternHi[A]; the pattern position (+$02) = 0; ReadPatternEvent $C2F6. A new entry: the cut had it inside OrderJumpSlot's block; it is ReadOrderList's JP Z target at $C324.
