$C3DA SlotRowOp ; ADD A,n: n = 8 x the channel (self-modified by UpdateTune $C212, $C24F, $C27B)
$C3DF ; the slot's record offset
$C3E6 ; IY = the record
$C3ED ; +8: the peak volume
$C3F3 ; the mixer: channel A bits 0 and 3
$C40C SetInstrumentB ; channel B: bits 1 and 4
$C41F SetInstrumentC ; channel C: bits 2 and 5
$C42D SetInstrumentEnvelope ; the attack: +3's high nibble through AttackRates
$C452 SetInstrumentSlowAttack ; bit 7: one step every n frames
$C45B SetInstrumentSustain ; +4's high nibble: the sustain level; the decay: +3's low nibble
$C485 SetInstrumentSlowDecay ; bit 7: one step every n frames
$C48E SetInstrumentRelease ; the release: +4's low nibble through DecayRates
$C4AE SetInstrumentSlowRelease ; bit 7: one step every n frames
$C4B7 SetInstrumentTimes ; +5 the gate-off time, +7 the vibrato

$C4C9 c StartNote ; Start note A: its period, the gate and the envelope, its duration, the vibrato, the arpeggio and the slide delay
> A = the note (0-$7F), DE = the pattern, from PatternEvent $C36D. The period-table index (+$1C) = A + 20 + the transpose (+$01); the period (+$1D/+$1E) = PeriodLo/PeriodHi[index] + the detune (+$09). The gate on, the volume and the envelope counters 0, the done bits of attack, decay and release clear. The next byte is the duration: the note timer (+$03). With a vibrato (+$0B not 0): its delay or cycles (+$0A) = the record's first byte, the step (+$0C) 1. With an arpeggio (+$10 not 0): the first hold (+$18) = ((header & $78) >> 3) + 1, the step (+$17) 1. The slide delay (+$14) again from the slide command (+$15). Returns to UpdateChannel's caller: no effects on a note's first frame.
> A new entry, for the cut's l_C4C9 inside OrderJumpSlot's block (PatternEvent's JP Z at $C36F).
> Witness: L1 15424 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C4DF ; + the detune
$C4E9 ; the gate on, the envelope from volume 0
$C506 ; the duration, kept in A' to the end
$C515 ; the vibrato: the record's first byte, from step 1
$C52A StartNoteArpeggio ; the arpeggio: the hold of the base note
$C548 StartNoteSlide ; the slide's delay again

@module effects ; The per-frame effects: the gate, the rest, the envelope, the vibrato, the arpeggio and the slide
@about The envelope (ChannelEffects $C55E) is the C64 ADSR in software: gate on, the volume climbs from 0 by the attack step at the attack rate to the instrument's peak, then falls by the decay step at the decay rate to the sustain level and holds; gate off (CheckGateOff $C555, when the note timer equals the gate-off time, 2 in every instrument: 2 frames before the note's end), it falls by the release step at the release rate to 0. With a release of 1 step every 5 frames the release never steps in tune 0 (its code $C5F0 was not executed in any of the 34 recordings).
@about The vibrato (VibratoEffect $C609): the record (VibratoTable-8 + the instrument's +7) holds a first byte and 7 signed period deltas. First byte with bit 7 clear: a delay in frames before the vibrato starts, then it runs to the note's end; with bit 7: the number of full cycles (bits 0-6) it runs. Each frame adds the next delta (step 1-7) to the period, with its sign turned over on every other pass of 7 (bit 7 of the step), so one cycle is 14 frames. The arpeggio (ArpeggioEffect $C694): the record (ArpeggioTable + 8n) is a header (bit 7 loop, bits 3-6 the first hold, bits 0-2 the count of steps) and steps (bits 3-7 semitones over the note, bits 0-2 the hold in frames, 0: 256); each step sets the period to the note plus its semitones (and the detune); at the end it loops (the base note held (header >> 3) & 7 frames first) or returns to the base note. The slide (SlideEffect $C72F): after its delay, the period goes up or down by half the step each frame for the count. Each of the three overwrites or moves the period the note set; the arpeggio's step overwrites what the vibrato and the slide did.

$C555 c CheckGateOff ; Gate off when the note timer reaches the gate-off time; then the effects
> A = the note timer (from UpdateChannel $C2E4). A = +$06: the gate bit (+$2A bit 0) clear: the release. Falls into ChannelEffects.
> Witness: L1 235309 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

$C55E c ChannelEffects ; The rest timer, the note timer and the envelope, then the vibrato, the arpeggio and the slide
> A rest (timer +$16 not 0): one less; at 0 the note timer 0 (the next event next frame); no effects. Else the note timer one less; NoteEndFlag $C14D up: return. Gate on: the attack (every rate frames, the volume + the step, to the peak), then the decay (to the sustain level). Gate off: the release (to 0). Then VibratoEffect $C609 (fall through).
> Witness: L1 235385 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C564 ; a rest: count it; at 0 its end
$C56D ChannelEffectsNote ; the note's timer
$C570 ; a note ended this frame: no effects
$C575 ; the gate: off, the release
$C57B ; the attack done: the decay
$C5A7 EnvelopeAttackStore ; the attack's new volume
$C5AC EnvelopeDecay ; the decay done: the sustain holds
$C5C9 EnvelopeSustain ; at the sustain level: the decay done
$C5D5 EnvelopeDecayStore ; not below the sustain level yet
$C5DF EnvelopeRelease ; the release done: nothing
$C606 EnvelopeReleaseStore ; the release's new volume

$C609 c VibratoEffect ; The vibrato: after its delay, the next of 7 period deltas, its sign flipped every other pass
> A new entry: the end of the envelope, where all its paths join (10 jumps to $C609 and the fall from $C606), and the start of the vibrato. No vibrato (+$0B = 0): ArpeggioEffect $C694. The delay or cycles byte (+$0A): bit 7 clear and not 0: one less, no step this frame; 0: step; bit 7 set: step until its low 7 bits are 0. A step: delta = (VibratoTable-8)[+$0B + (step & $7F)] (CommandParam $C1E0 holds its size): the period + delta while the step's bit 7 is clear, the period - delta while it is set. After step 7 the step becomes $81 (bit 7 flipped, step 1); after the flipped pass's step 7, 1 again: a cycle done, and a cycles count one less.
> Records 4, 5 and 7 use it (VibratoTable's only record: delay 40). The cycles form ($C61A), and a delta that carries or borrows in the period ($C654, $C670) was not executed in any of the 34 recordings.
> Witness: L1 208864 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C620 VibratoDelay ; the delay one less
$C626 VibratoStep ; the delta of this step
$C648 VibratoDown ; the period - the size
$C659 VibratoPositive ; a positive delta: up unless the step's bit 7
$C665 VibratoUp ; the period + the size
$C673 VibratoNext ; the next step; after 7 the sign flips ($89)

$C694 c ArpeggioEffect ; The arpeggio: when the hold ends, the next step's note and hold
> No arpeggio (+$10 = 0): SlideEffect $C72F. The hold (+$18) one less; not 0: SlideEffect. Step (+$17) 1-7: the byte at ArpeggioTable + 8n + step: the hold = its bits 0-2, the period = the note (+$1C) + its bits 3-7 + the detune. Step 0 (a looped arpeggio's restart): the header's bits 3-5 as the hold of the base note (when not 0). After the last step (the header's bits 0-2): 0 when the header's bit 7 is set (loop), else $FF; $FF at the hold's end: the base note again and $FE, after which nothing.
> Arpeggios 1-6 ran (patterns 2, 7-9, 13, 16, 18, 19). The end ($C70E) was not executed in any of the 34 recordings: arpeggio 1, the only one with no loop, plays on 9-frame notes, which end first.
> Witness: L1 208864 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C6C1 ArpeggioByte ; the step's byte
$C6C2 ArpeggioApply ; the hold and the semitones over the note
$C6EC ; the next step; after the last: 0 (loop) or $FF (end)
$C708 ArpeggioSetStep ; 0 or $FF
$C70E ArpeggioEnd ; $FF: back to the base note, then $FE

$C72F c SlideEffect ; The slide: after its delay, the period up or down by half the step, for the count
> A new entry: ArpeggioEffect's paths join here (5 jumps to $C72F and the fall from $C72C). The delay (+$14) not 0: one less. Else with a count (+$11 not 0; $FF endless, else one less): the step (+$12/+$13) halved; the slide command's bit 5 (+$15) set: the period + step/2 (the pitch falls); clear: the period - step/2 - the step's bit 0 (SBC with the carry RR C left). Returns to UpdateTune $C1E4.
> Ran in no recording past the delay test: tune 0 has no slide ($C735-$C77C not executed in any of the 34 recordings).
> Witness: L1 208864 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C73A SlideCount ; the count: 0 none, $FF endless
$C747 SlideApply ; the direction: bit 5 of the command
$C767 SlideUp ; the period - step/2: the pitch rises
$C77F SlideDone

@module player
$C780 c EndTune ; The order list's $FF: silence, PlayerState 0, the AY written, the frame over
> From ReadOrderList $C31F. The three volumes (+$1F) 0 (each written twice), PlayerState $C027 = 0, UpdateChannel's return dropped (POP AF: the channels after this one are not updated), then WriteAY $C290 with H = $FF, L = $BF, C = $FD, whatever NoteEndFlag. MusicTick's next call starts tune 0 again (StartTune $C79F): the frame after.
> Ran at frame 9581 in explorers and once in r08000, r18000, r28000, r38000 and r48000, 9698 frames apart.
> Witness: L1 6 (explorers, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

$C79F c StartTune ; Start tune A: its entry, the empty patterns, the channel records cleared, PlayerState 1
> A = the tune (0-3; always 0: MusicTick's JP Z at $C018 is the only way in). TuneNumberOp+1 = A (channel C is written only for tune 0); TunePointer $C14B = TuneTable $C967 + 6A; PatternPointers $C1DA = EmptyPattern $C82D for all three; ChannelA-ChannelC ($C153-$C1D9) zero; PlayerState $C027 = 1. A is kept. SlotTable, MixerImage and the AY are not touched; nothing sounds this frame.
> Ran once in c1 (frame 21599), once in explorers (9582) and after each EndTune in the rzx pieces.
> Witness: L1 7 (c1, explorers, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$C7A3 ; HL = 6 x A
$C7B1 ; every channel on the empty pattern
$C7BD ; the three channel records zero

@module channel
$C7D1 c SetDetune ; Order command $C0: the next byte is the channel's detune (+$09)
> Then ReadOrderList $C310. Tune 0's channel B: $C0 10 at its start, $C0 0 after the intro (pattern 5); a constant added to every period (and so a lower pitch, a little, for the 10).
> Witness: L1 17 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
